            <h4 class="font-bold text-xl text-gray-900 mb-2">Does Menards carry the same brands as Home Depot?</h4>
            <p class="text-gray-700">There's overlap — both stock Rust-Oleum EPOXYSHIELD and Henry products — but Menards also carries regional brands like Gardner and Quikrete's dual-surface sealer. Check current in-store stock, since selection shifts through the season at both chains.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h4 class="font-bold text-xl text-gray-900 mb-2">How much driveway sealer should I buy at Menards?</h4>
            <p class="text-gray-700">Asphalt sealers typically come in 4.75-gallon pails covering 300–400 sq ft per coat. A standard two-car driveway (~600 sq ft) usually needs two pails for a first-time two-coat job, or often one pail for a single-coat maintenance reseal.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h4 class="font-bold text-xl text-gray-900 mb-2">Can I use a concrete sealer on my asphalt driveway?</h4>
            <p class="text-gray-700">No, with one exception: dual-rated products like Quikrete Concrete & Asphalt Sealer are formulated for both. Standard acrylic concrete sealers won't bond with or protect asphalt, and asphalt emulsion won't adhere properly to concrete.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h4 class="font-bold text-xl text-gray-900 mb-2">Is it worth waiting for a rebate before buying driveway sealer at Menards?</h4>
            <p class="text-gray-700">If your project timeline allows it, checking the current rebate percentage before buying is worth the few minutes it takes — the effective savings can be substantial on a multi-pail purchase for a large driveway. Just weigh that against your actual weather window; delaying a purchase to catch a slightly better rebate isn't worth missing the dry, warm stretch you need for the job to cure properly.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h4 class="font-bold text-xl text-gray-900 mb-2">Does Menards price-match driveway sealer against other retailers?</h4>
            <p class="text-gray-700">Menards' price-match policies vary by store and change periodically, so confirm current policy with your local store before assuming a specific match will apply. It's worth asking about in-store if you've seen the same product priced lower elsewhere, particularly during the competitive spring sealing season when several chains run overlapping seasonal promotions.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h4 class="font-bold text-xl text-gray-900 mb-2">What time of year does Menards stock the most driveway sealer?</h4>
            <p class="text-gray-700">Selection is widest from late spring through mid-summer, matching the ideal warm, dry application window for most products. Stock thins out heading into fall and largely disappears over winter, so plan a spring shopping trip if you want the full lineup this guide covers rather than whatever's left on clearance in September.</p>
